1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:10,000
DeepMind Technologies Limited, trading as Google DeepMind or simply DeepMind, is a British-American artificial intelligence (AI) research laboratory which serves as a subsidiary of Alphabet

2
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:20,000
Inc. Founded in the UK in 2010, it was acquired by Google in 2014,[8] and merged with Google AI's Google Brain division to become Google

3
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:30,000
DeepMind in April 2023. The company is headquartered in London, with research centres in the United States, Canada,[9] France,[10] Germany, and Switzerland. In 2014, DeepMind

4
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:40,000
introduced neural Turing machines (neural networks that can access external memory like a conventional Turing machine).[11][12] The company has created many neural network models trained

5
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:50,000
with reinforcement learning to play video games and board games. It made headlines in 2016 after its AlphaGo program beat Lee Sedol, a Go world

6
00:00:50,000 --> 00:01:00,000
champion, in a five-game match, which was later featured in the documentary AlphaGo.[13] A more general program, AlphaZero, beat the most powerful programs playing go,

7
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:10,000
chess and shogi (Japanese chess) after a few days of play against itself using reinforcement learning.[14] DeepMind has since trained models for game-playing (MuZero, AlphaStar),

8
00:01:10,000 --> 00:01:20,000
for mathematics (AlphaGeometry, FunSearch), and for algorithm discovery (AlphaEvolve, AlphaDev, AlphaTensor). In 2020, DeepMind made significant advances in the problem of protein folding with AlphaFold,

9
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:30,000
which achieved state of the art records on benchmark tests for protein folding prediction.[15] In July 2022, it was announced that over 200 million predicted

10
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:40,000
protein structures, representing virtually all known proteins, would be released on the AlphaFold database.[16][17] Google DeepMind has become responsible for the development of Gemini (Google's

11
00:01:40,000 --> 00:01:50,000
family of large language models) and other generative AI tools, such as the text-to-image model Imagen, the text-to-video model Veo, and the text-to-music model Lyria.
